			</span>
		</div>
		<div class="h6 mt-lg-5">
			In the video, the image on the left shows the 2D map; you can see rays shooting from the player 
			until they hit an object forming the field of view, while the image on the right shows the ray-cast image. Similar to the 
			HOW section, imagine all the white squares have a value of 1, letting the program know, "This 
			should be a red wall." Except for the one blue wall, which would have a different value to let 
			the program know, "This should be a blue wall"
		</div>
